# G112 — Backup Script Maker

*v2. See `backup-script-maker.md` for prose: shell-safe quoting, validation
before emit, YAML spec as data shape, dialect-specific DDL via resolver.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Scheduled Backups

[scheduled-backups @config-glob
    IN ORDER TO
        read backup config yaml, validate, emit a shell script
        install a cron entry, and surface errors without writing bad scripts

    @configs <- [vault[read-configs {glob: @config-glob}]]

    for @config in @configs
        @spec <- [bsm[spec-from-yaml {yaml: @config:content}]]
        @result <- [bsm[emit-script {spec: @spec}]]

        @result
            where errors is empty
            IN ORDER TO
                write the script to disk with mode 0755
                and install a 2am daily cron entry
            [vault[save {path: "backup-scripts/" + @spec:database + ".sh",
                          content: @result:script, mode: 0755}]]
            [cron[install {schedule: "0 2 * * *",
                            script: "backup-scripts/" + @spec:database + ".sh"}]]
            || [ui[show-errors {config: @config:path,
                                 errors: @result:errors}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[bsm
    spec              {database}              ;; with defaults
    spec-from-yaml    {yaml}
    validate          {spec}                   ;; -> [validation-error]
    shell-quote       {str}
    emit-script       {spec}                   ;; || validation-errors
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: shell-quote as safety discipline

[bsm[shell-quote {str: @s}
    where
        result is single-quoted
        and embedded single quotes are escaped as '\''
        so that no shell metacharacter is ever interpreted
]

Every path and value from config flows through `shell-quote` before
concatenation into the script. The v1 insight "never concatenate raw
strings into shell scripts" becomes a `where`-documented invariant.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @spec <- [bsm[spec-from-yaml
                    {yaml: "database: projects\nhost: 127.0.0.1\nport: 5432\n"}]]
    -> [bsm[validate {spec: @spec}]]        ;; -> []

    @script <- [bsm[emit-script {spec: @spec}]]
    -> @script:script contains "pg_dump"     ;; -> true
    -> @script:script contains "'projects'"  ;; -> true (shell-quoted)
]
